<title>SWEDEN: Swedish T-bill auction oversubscribed.</title>
<headline>Swedish T-bill auction oversubscribed.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>An auction of three- and six-month T-bills was oversubscribed, the National Debt Office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The average accepted rate in an auction of three-month T-bills worth 4.35 billion crowns ($644.3 million) was 3.99 percent, the debt office said.</p>
<p>The office received 35 bids worth 5.5 billion crowns, of which it accepted 31 bids.</p>
<p>An auction of six-month paper worth 3.0 billion crowns received 40 bids worth 6.75 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The average accepted rate was 4.04 percent, the office said. -- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017 ($ = 6.751 Norwegian Crowns)</p>
</text>
